<title>Lesson Activities </title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item>2.9.1: Writing Solutions to Inequalities</item>
  <item>2.9.2: Graphing Inequalities<list>
      <item>2.9.2: Self Check </item>
      <item>2.9.2: Additional Resources </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>2.9.3: Understanding the Meaning of an Inequality<list>
      <item>2.9.3: Self Check </item>
      <item>2.9.3: Additional Resources </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>2.9.4: Making Sense of Inequalities and Their Solutions </item>
  <item>2.9.5: Comparing Equality and Inequality<list>
      <item>2.9.5: Self Check </item>
      <item>2.9.5: Additional Resources </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>2.9.6: Using Technology to Visualize Inequality Solutions </item>
  <item>2.9.7: Identifying Inequality Solutions on a Graph</item>
</list>
<para> Students will also complete a series of problems in the 2.9.8: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item>None</item> 
</list>
<title>Required Preparation </title>
<para>Devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology are needed.</para>


